<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">30052026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Israel has ordered its military to occupy seventy percent of Gaza, far beyond the fifty-three percent cap set by the US-brokered ceasefire.</s> <s>UN figures show Israeli forces already control sixty percent of the enclave, confining two point three million Palestinians, half of them children, to barely a third of the land.</s> <s>Germany, Israel's second-largest arms supplier, says it opposes permanent division — but Netanyahu has hinted he may push further still.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Iran and the United States are closing in on a framework to reopen the Strait of Hormuz, the channel that carries one-fifth of the world's oil.</s> <s>Tehran is demanding the immediate return of twelve billion dollars in frozen assets, and warns that Washington declared the deal done before Iran ever agreed.</s> <s>Mediators across the Muslim world, not Europe, shuttled the proposals between capitals — a quiet shift in who arbitrates the Middle East.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Russian Geran drone slammed into an apartment block in Galați, Romania, the first of twenty-eight airspace violations to wound civilians.</s> <s>NATO condemned the strike as reckless rather than deliberate, but the distinction offers little comfort to a member state now under fire.</s> <s>Bucharest summoned Russia's ambassador and requested faster anti-drone defences before the next incursion.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Islamic State's Sahel Province claimed its first-ever attack inside Nigeria, saying it killed nineteen people in the north-west.</s> <s>That region had long been ruled by criminal bandit militias, not jihadist groups, and the claim signals a dangerous merging of the two.</s> <s>Nigeria's military hasn't confirmed the deaths, and the blurring line between banditry and ideology is exactly what makes the threat so hard to fight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A US Immigration and Customs Enforcement agent, Christian Castro, was arrested over a shooting in Minneapolis this January.</s> <s>Castro fired through a front door, wounding a Venezuelan man named Julio Sosa-Celis, then falsely claimed three men had beaten him with shovels.</s> <s>Texas Governor Abbott must now decide whether to extradite him — a test of whether the agency's own officers answer to the law they enforce.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India's weather agency now puts the odds of drought at sixty percent, with El Niño forecast to strengthen from weak in June to severe by September.</s> <s>More than half the country's farmland is rain-fed, so a failed monsoon would delay sowing across the fields that feed hundreds of millions.</s> <s>Whether the rains come as hoped, God willing, will shape food prices for the world's most populous nation.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Forty-two thousand HIV patients in Pakistan face gaps in treatment as global health aid collapses.</s> <s>The country spends just nine-tenths of one percent of its economy on public health, and donor money long covered the surveillance and supply chains the state never funded.</s> <s>In Balochistan, the tuberculosis programme now faces an eighty percent funding shortfall — a quiet emergency measured in lives, not headlines.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Russian drone set a Turkish-owned freighter ablaze off Odesa, wounding two crew members.</s> <s>The Black Sea export corridor, underwritten by Turkey, ships grain to food-import-dependent nations, and every strike on it pushes freight insurance higher.</s> <s>Ankara has stayed silent on the attack against its own vessel, even as the cost ripples toward the world's poorest importers.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Kenya's courts have halted a US plan to offload Ebola patients into a facility built on Kenyan soil.</s> <s>Washington refused to repatriate the cases to its own specialized biocontainment hospitals, choosing instead to construct a centre abroad.</s> <s>With the World Health Organization counting more than one thousand Ebola cases in neighbouring Congo, a hearing on June second will decide the facility's fate.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The refrigerants that cool our homes warm the planet thousands of times faster than carbon dioxide, the UN Environment Programme warns.</s> <s>Global demand for cooling could triple by twenty-fifty, concentrated in the Global South where rules for safely disposing of those chemicals are weakest.</s> <s>Which chemistry fills that coming wave of air conditioners is still undecided, and the climate hangs on the answer.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Astronomers have found a supermassive black hole hidden behind thick dust in the Antennae galaxies, where two spirals are colliding.</s> <s>As gas falls inward during such mergers, it generates dust that masks the feeding black hole at visible wavelengths, disguising its growth as ordinary star formation.</s> <s>The finding is still a preprint, unconfirmed by peer review, and X-ray or radio surveys could yet settle it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Classical computers have just solved a benchmark problem in quantum chemistry that was meant to showcase quantum machines.</s> <s>Chemistry has long been called the killer application that would justify quantum computing commercially, so the result narrows where quantum truly beats the ordinary.</s> <s>Just how many chemistry problems still demand a quantum computer remains an open, and very valuable, question.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Police in the Netherlands dismantled a botnet of seventeen million hijacked devices, reportedly tied to a Russia-based service called ASOCKS.</s> <s>The network rented out ordinary people's infected phones and routers as anonymous proxies, masking criminal traffic behind innocent home connections.</s> <s>How seventeen million devices were ever enrolled remains unknown, and so does where their operators have fled.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pope Leo the Fourteenth has issued an encyclical declaring that technology is never neutral, calling artificial intelligence a commercial product that concentrates power.</s> <s>The document demands oversight wherever AI touches fundamental rights, a rare moral intervention from a global institution.</s> <s>Yet its framework is steeped in Catholicism, leaving the faiths of most of humanity, including the Muslim world, absent from the rooms where AI's guardrails are written.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A security researcher published working exploits for unpatched Microsoft flaws on GitHub, forcing the company's hand.</s> <s>Releasing live code pressures vendors to patch faster, but it also opens a window where attackers and defenders hold exactly the same weapon.</s> <s>The researcher has threatened more releases, and Microsoft still won't say when the holes will be closed.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>